From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:33:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build KGSL against the RetroidPocket 7.3 mainline kernel

Mechanical port of Qualcomm's graphics-kernel (as shipped in LineageOS
sm8750 modules, kernel 6.6 era) to mainline 7.3, enough to build
msm_kgsl.ko out of tree. Untested on hardware.

Kernel API changes handled:
- platform_driver.remove returns void
- MODULE_IMPORT_NS() takes a string
- dma_fence_ops lost fence_value_str/timeline_value_str/use_64bit_seqno
  (64-bit seqno now comes from dma_fence_init64()), __dma_fence_is_later()
  takes the fence, dma_fence_array_create() lost signal-on-any
- mm->get_unmapped_area became mm_get_unmapped_area(), and
  __get_unmapped_area() is no longer exported
- dma_buf_attachment.dma_map_attrs is gone
- iommu_domain_alloc(bus) became iommu_paging_domain_alloc(dev)
- thermal_of_cooling_device_register() takes a cooling device id
- bin_attribute callbacks take a const attribute
- del_timer*() renamed timer_delete*(), nth_page() removed,
  drivers/devfreq/governor.h became linux/devfreq-governor.h

Downstream-only kernel features, stubbed in compat/ (all optional for
plain rendering): qcom-iommu-util and qcom io-pgtable (context bank is
always 0 on mainline arm-smmu-qcom), msm_hw_fence/synx, TZ GPU DCVS
SCM calls, qcom_dcvs L3 voting, socinfo part info, mem-buf/secure
buffers, minidump, sysstats, msm_performance. SCM calls with a mainline
equivalent are mapped (gpu smmu aperture, gpu init regs, pas shutdown).

config/rp6.conf: kalama settings without coresight and with the
simple_ondemand devfreq governor, selected with KGSL_RP6=y.
